{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations","id":1541002,"title":"Pre-Existent Souls and Moonchild Operations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-25T14:27:31-07:00","id":1541002,"title":"Pre-Existent Souls and Moonchild Operations","content":"Following are a series of thoughts regarding the Arcana involved in incarnating a soul. For the sake of discussion, two processes are primarily discussed. The first is that of attaching a soul to a natural pregnancy, whether that be the mage's own pregnancy or that of a target. The second is that of incarnating a soul into a living construct that has been manifested ahead of time using other Arcana. There are of course, even more esoteric processes that come to mind, like giving souls to machine intelligences, but I have largely limited my thoughts on the matter to those two modes.<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, it would seem like the Arcanum involved in incarnation itself would be Death. The 1e write-up mentioned how Death attracted the soul into matter, and Death as a whole has generally been depicted as the Arcanum that deals with souls. It seems like Death 4 would be required to permanently affix a soul to a Pattern, whether that be the Pattern of an unborn child or that of a human fashioned through the use of the Life Arcanum. I cannot really see Death 5 being involved, given how no Making is involved, but I can also see why some Storytellers would want that level of proficiency in the Arcanum being required.<br /> <br /> A significant question, though, is whether or not use of the Mind Arcanum would also be required if one desired a fully functional human being to manifest. In the case of a natural pregnancy, it seems like it would not be necessary, but I can see an artificial human requiring the application of the Mind Arcanum to demonstrate sapience.<br /> <br /> Of course, constructing a living body would probably be Life 5, given the use of Making.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T12:52:04-07:00","id":1541030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations#post1541002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1e write-up mentioned how Death attracted the soul into matter, and Death as a whole has generally been depicted as the Arcanum that deals with souls. It seems like Death 4 would be required to permanently affix a soul to a Pattern, whether that be the Pattern of an unborn child or that of a human fashioned through the use of the Life Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually only requires Death 2 to affix souls to anything, although it required one Reach to bind it to a soulless human and two Reach to make the effect Lasting.<br /> <br /> I do question why you'd use magic to steal another person's soul and give it to a foetus when that newborn is going to get their own soul naturally anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see an artificial human requiring the application of the Mind Arcanum to demonstrate sapience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Second Edition book is pretty direct about the fact that, yes, an entity created through a Making of Life will not have a consciousness unless a mind is also created for them with the appropriate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> That's not even just for humans; any animal created with Life alone will have less of what might be considered a mind than naturally occurring examples of its kind. The extent to which that matters will differ, but it will probably be quite apparent in most mammals and birds and more than a few reptiles.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually starting to think of how it would manifest in birds, since they're something I've been looking at a lot lately and reading more into the fact that they're fairly smart and often highly social. The way I'm imagining one that would come off as though it would lack those traits is actually pretty disturbing.) <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T14:02:59-07:00","id":1541033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541030#post1541030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually only requires Death 2 to affix souls to anything, although it required one Reach to bind it to a soulless human and two Reach to make the effect Lasting.<br /> <br /> I do question why you'd use magic to steal another person's soul and give it to a foetus when that newborn is going to get their own soul naturally anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, the Second Edition book is pretty direct about the fact that, yes, an entity created through a Making of Life will not have a consciousness unless a mind is also created for them with the appropriate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> That's not even just for humans; any animal created with Life alone will have less of what might be considered a mind than naturally occurring examples of its kind. The extent to which that matters will differ, but it will probably be quite apparent in most mammals and birds and more than a few reptiles.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually starting to think of how it would manifest in birds, since they're something I've been looking at a lot lately and reading more into the fact that they're fairly smart and often highly social. The way I'm imagining one that would come off as though it would lack those traits is actually pretty disturbing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not known that attaching a soul to an object was only Death 2, actually. That is understandable, though, since the Soul Jar Rote is also Death 2. In regards to the soul used, I originally thought of using pre-existent souls rather than the souls of the deceased. Of course, that still leaves the question of why one would bother with using magic to do so when a soul would just naturally incarnate in a child anyway.<br /> <br /> You also raise a good point about the relative degree of consciousness in organisms fashioned using Life. I was under the impression that they were entirely mindless, and would thus die without care. Do such organisms actually possess rudimentary instincts, even if they do not possess self-awareness?<br /> <br /> You also raise a good point in regards to social animals. It is sort of hard to imagine how a mindless bird would even interact with the environment. I am guessing that the disconnect between naturally-born and Life-grown animals of the same species would be more pronounced among vertebrates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T15:39:46-07:00","id":1541036,"title":"","content":"If the goal is just creating a soul, you would need the constituent parts working in sync/holistically with each other, so at a minimum that's Death, Fate, Prime, Mind, and Spirit at 6 dots for the practice of Dynamics, and realistically at 8 dots for the practice of Dominions.<br /> <br /> Not sure how interested I am in the rest of the thought experiment, but wanted to comment on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T06:42:02-07:00","id":1541124,"title":"","content":"What are Moonchild operations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T15:09:32-07:00","id":1541662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541036#post1541036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the goal is just creating a soul, you would need the constituent parts working in sync/holistically with each other, so at a minimum that's Death, Fate, Prime, Mind, and Spirit at 6 dots for the practice of Dynamics, and realistically at 8 dots for the practice of Dominions.<br /> <br /> Not sure how interested I am in the rest of the thought experiment, but wanted to comment on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering the problem of implanting an unborn soul from somewhere else into a body. In this case, it would not be creating all of the parts from scratch, but rather implanting it into an organism. I think that you might be onto something though in regards to other Arcana coming into play when it comes to having the soul integrate with the body and mind. I do not remember if restoring souls to Sleepers actually required anything beyond Death, though, which feels like the most analogous situation. The necessity of Fate is interesting, though. Maybe it would not just be used for the timing of the actual working but it would also work the being into the fabric of destiny so that they are not disconnected? As an aside, I am not very familiar with the rules for Archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T15:19:12-07:00","id":1541663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541124#post1541124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Moonchild operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of the sorts of magical operations that are intended to implant a non-human intelligence into a human body. I just mentioned the Moonchild operation that Crowley popularized because it is well-known. The Moonchild operation involved the incarnation of a spirit in the unborn child of a pregnant woman, and so it would cover the sort of spells involving natural pregnancies that I mentioned, but it would not really align with spells that involve the creation of a fully-grown living body. I did not intend for the discussion to be limited to that sort of operation, I just mentioned it as it gets the idea across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T18:14:59-07:00","id":1541669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541662#post1541662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was considering the problem of implanting an unborn soul from somewhere else into a body. In this case, it would not be creating all of the parts from scratch, but rather implanting it into an organism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just Death. It's the Reach effect of Soul Jar to attach the soul to a person with one of the soul loss conditions. The problem you're going to run into with &quot;unborn souls&quot; is that in ChroD metaphysics the systems object referred to as a soul instantiates at birth. The sidebar for the sympathetic connections of an unborn child can be used for affecting them with magic as usual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that you might be onto something though in regards to other Arcana coming into play when it comes to having the soul integrate with the body and mind. I do not remember if restoring souls to Sleepers actually required anything beyond Death, though, which feels like the most analogous situation. The necessity of Fate is interesting, though. Maybe it would not just be used for the timing of the actual working but it would also work the being into the fabric of destiny so that they are not disconnected? As an aside, I am not very familiar with the rules for Archmastery. </div> </div> </div>The Practice of Dynamics, the first Imperial Practice archmasters get to grips with, is used to create spells that dynamically alter themselves in response to different conditions, vary in effects based on who encounters them, and otherwise update themselves without Awakened oversight. The Practice of Dominions, the last Imperial Practice that is both well-defined in its effects and confirmed to exist, is the one archmasters use to create subsouls like ochemata or Chantries from their own souls.<br /> <br /> The soul the Awakened work with is canonically made up of the five Subtle Arcana plus some special sauce that the Tremere attribute to the Sixth and Seventh Watchtowers; Mummy likewise describes the soul as being the product of binding the five powers together, with the undifferentiated stuff of manifest existence both differentiating into those powers and no longer holding them together once the soul disappears upon death without magical assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T12:50:45-07:00","id":1541696,"title":"","content":"I have a vague recollection that Imperial Mysteries posited the means of creating a soul ex nihilo as an enduring mystery even for archmasters. I think that can hold up even if one thinks it should be within the capacity of even the least of the Imperial Practices, given the conceit of quintessences; the exclusivity is the kind of thing that can be used to maintain many examples of spells that could be theoretically cast but as yet none of the handful of archmasters has managed to either divine or acquire the components necessary to actually bring about.<br /> <br /> Although I'll admit, it is a bit funny how the game treats the soul as a bit sacrosanct in that regard, given how it's otherwise a bit irreverent on the topic. Sure, the soul is integral to a person being fully functional, but in the same way a vital organ can be (including the fact that it can be replaced with one that came from another). But it's not positioned as the truest and most essential aspect or form of a person, and the very notion of an afterlife is still an open question. As it is, the most concrete thing that comes out of obstacles for mages to create one is creating complications and moral quandaries for resurrection, conjuring entire new humans, and dealing with the aftermath of Reapers (or anybody who might latch on to the idea that rendering a mage soulless is the most sure way to disable their powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T13:46:16-07:00","id":1541699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541696#post1541696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a vague recollection that Imperial Mysteries posited the means of creating a soul ex nihilo as an enduring mystery even for archmasters.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>IM</i> has creating a soul as a 7 dot Death spell. I suspect you're thinking of the section on the Principle, which states that archmasters aren't sure where all the souls in the world come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T17:47:54-07:00","id":1541715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541699#post1541699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>IM</i> has creating a soul as a 7 dot Death spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably that's creating a <i>replacement</i> soul \u2014 &quot;create a new soul for a target that has lost their own&quot; isn't creating bespoke novelty souls to spec the way subsouls approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T05:41:42-07:00","id":1541773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541715#post1541715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably that's creating a <i>replacement</i> soul \u2014 &quot;create a new soul for a target that has lost their own&quot; isn't creating bespoke novelty souls to spec the way subsouls approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Subsouls are also just parts of the Oversoul of the archmage/ascended being, in the same sense they would not be bespoke and novel right? The Archmaster is using something which they already have to create a subsoul...<br /> <br /> Whereas we know the Principle - via Prometheans - create souls Alchemically (in a process of immense story telling challenge...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T10:12:15-07:00","id":1541785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1541002-pre-existent-souls-and-moonchild-operations?p=1541699#post1541699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>IM</i> has creating a soul as a 7 dot Death spell. I suspect you're thinking of the section on the Principle, which states that archmasters aren't sure where all the souls in the world come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I was just conflating some things Malcolm said from Imperial Mysteries and Left-Hand Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:52:38-07:00","id":1541819,"title":"","content":"I think that mages not knowing whether or not souls can be created or not was only established in a sidebar in the 2e core rulebook. There was little on the topic in 1e, apart from the idea that souls fell into the Fallen World from the Supernal World. Some of the text seemed to imply that souls had some point of origination, but the book did not come to close to making a definitive statement on the topic. The one thing that was pretty solid was the soul has to have some form of pre-existence in the Supernal World, as it was trapped in the Fallen World after the Abyss reared its head. Of course, the construct which the game refers to by the term soul would not really align all of the ideas of incarnation magic that have been discussed in this thread. Perhaps Mind would be the key factor then, given its ties to identity? Other than that, it still seems like it is possible that the soul would be a relevant factor in a working that is modelled after a classic Moonchild operation or the like. According to the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook, you need a soul in order to utilize Supernatural Merits, and obviously you need a soul in order to Awaken, even if you can retain your magic should your soul get stolen. As an aside, I almost feel like such a working could be used as flavor for a Proximi Dynasty or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}